<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conrad II, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 990–1039</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Conrad II was the first Salian king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, elected in 1024 and crowned emperor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 1027. He put down the revolt of his stepson Duke Ernest II of Swabia, granted counties in the Alpine valleys to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trento">Trent</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brixen">Brixen</a> to secure the routes to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, and in 1032 inherited the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arles">Arles</a>. In Italy he confirmed the hereditary rights of lesser <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/conrad-ii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Conrad II, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="465" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Conrad_II_(HRE).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
